destination: Nix development shells run as first-class sandboxed environments on Linux and macOS, confined in user space by bubblewrap and App Sandbox respectively, with no virtualisation
created: 2026-10-31
tickets[11]{id,question,blockers,state,answer,evidence}:
  T-001,"Can the App Sandbox entitlement API confine an unsigned devShell binary?",,answered,"No for the entitlement API: it requires a signed bundle. The spike exercised the sandbox_init entry point with a Seatbelt profile",evidence/T-001.md
  T-002,"Does the sandbox_init entry point confine an unsigned binary with a Seatbelt profile on a current macOS?",,answered,"Yes. sandbox_init applies a Seatbelt profile and confines the adhoc-signed binary; this is not entitlement-based App Sandbox support",evidence/T-002.md
  T-003,"Is bwrap viable as an unprivileged Linux sandbox?",,answered,"Yes. It builds the sandbox from unprivileged user namespaces, with no root and no daemon",evidence/T-003.md
  T-004,"Can the host Nix store be shared without copying?",,answered,"Yes for integrity and deduplication: a read-only bind exposes the same immutable paths. Confidentiality is not implied",evidence/T-004.md
  T-005,"Can bwrap restrict egress by destination?",,answered,"No. An unshared network namespace has loopback only; host filtering needs a proxy",evidence/T-005.md
  T-006,"Does confinement require virtualisation?",,answered,"No. Both mechanisms enforce in the shared kernel",evidence/T-006.md
  T-007,"Can lifecycle work without a supervisor?",,answered,"Partially: process groups give group-local pause, resume and kill. A setsid child survives destroy, stays confined but can still use CPU or write granted paths. Complete lifecycle is unresolved",evidence/T-007.md
  T-008,"Do the target distributions permit unprivileged user namespaces?",,answered,"Yes on NixOS and Fedora; Ubuntu 24.04 blocks by default and allows when the AppArmor and clone sysctls are relaxed. Verified in VMs",evidence/T-008.md
  T-009,"Can lifecycle use --new-session with cgroup v2 freeze on systemd hosts and process-group signalling elsewhere?",,answered,"Yes on systemd hosts with cgroup delegation: a transient user scope with freeze/thaw. The process-group launcher is the fallback",evidence/T-009.md
  T-010,"Can per-sandbox resource limits be applied without a long-lived supervisor?",,answered,"Yes on systemd: MemoryMax and TasksMax on the transient scope. The fallback runs unlimited",evidence/T-010.md
  T-011,"Can the devShell capture supply the environment allowlist?",,open,,
decision: "Adopt bubblewrap on Linux and App Sandbox via the sandbox_init entry point on macOS. The entitlement API requires a signed bundle, so unsigned devShell binaries use the deprecated entry point; its longevity is a carried risk. Process-group lifecycle is group-local: a setsid child survives destroy, so complete lifecycle management is unresolved; a systemd scope provides freeze/thaw and resource limits, with a process-group fallback. T-008 is answered on NixOS, Ubuntu and Fedora. Further carried risks: egress beyond loopback needs a proxy on both platforms, the devShell-derived environment allowlist remains open, and a user manager without cgroup delegation is accepted as an unverified host state where the scope start fails and the caller selects the process-group fallback."
adrs[2]:
  - adrs/2026-10-31-linux-bwrap-sandbox
  - adrs/2026-10-31-linux-bwrap-lifecycle
steps[8]{n,step,state}:
  1,"Spike bubblewrap confinement on Linux: fixture, minimal bind set, isolation assertions, lifecycle, diagnostics, user namespace probe (T-008) and cost",done
  2,"Productionise the Linux isolation module: typed view to argv, invariants, version floor, golden argv, fail closed",next
  3,"Add the Nix devShell provider: host-side activation capture, exec wrapper, store write model, private workspace and snapshots",pending
  4,"Lift the macOS helper from the Darwin spike into the same provider contract, reusing its SBPL renderer and lifecycle findings, with the deprecation risk documented",pending
  5,"Refactor the provider interface around environments: exec, spawn, file transfer, capability declaration and per-provider configuration",pending
  6,"Reach parity: ports, snapshot integration, CLI and MCP surface, documentation, and the platform risk of the macOS primitive",pending
  7,"Follow-up ADR: session isolation and resource limits. Copy this PoC, then add cgroup v2 freeze and limits on systemd hosts with a process-group fallback for hosts without it",done
  8,"Nix provider: derive the sandbox environment allowlist from the devShell capture, with a secret-name denylist",blocked
